    "created_at": "2020-01-03T14:36:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-03T14:36:05Z",
    "body": "Well, this is a conformance requirement, not a processing requirement. If there was a set of IDs pointer attribute it would never be able to match your ID with space, so flagging it as non-conforming seems helpful. That a non-set ID pointer attribute can still match it doesn't really matter for that, I think.",
