    "created_at": "2020-01-03T16:42:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-03T16:42:14Z",
    "body": "> I expect it's to allow a space-separated set of IDs to exist, but I don't really recall any attribute which has that.\r\n\r\nIn HTML itself, there are three:\r\n\r\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#attr-tdth-headers\r\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/microdata.html#attr-itemref\r\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#attr-output-for\r\n\r\n…and ARIA adds several more:\r\n\r\n* https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-controls\r\n* https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-describedby\r\n* https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-flowto\r\n* https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-labelledby",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
